# Physics catalog, native receipt (P4): adding a node under each law. `open`
# is the add gesture — a fresh node minted beside its origin — and the two
# donor contracts are what is checked: the structural change reheats the
# layout, and the newcomer is absorbed without any pair left overlapping.
# The laws are chosen by palette label, as a person would.
settle 40
act Open Arrange pane
settle 10
# Not maximized: a maximized Arrange pane hides the graph, whose canvas then
# never frames, so its layout read model would freeze mid-settle.
assert row Physics: Springs
# Free arrangement: an analytic one would anchor every body and hide the law.
act Layout: Force-directed
settle 5
assert row Arrangement: Free
# The canvas boots with the law running; assert it rather than toggling
# blind, because a paused canvas refuses every settle and an add would then
# never separate.
assert physics running

# --- Springs: the newcomer is absorbed and the ringing dies away ---
open mere://p4/add/springs
wait
assert nodes >= 2
assert overlaps == 0
capture 01_add_springs

# --- Orbit: restless, so the layout still carries energy ---
act Physics: Orbit
settle 60
assert row Physics: Orbit
open mere://p4/add/orbit
wait
# Energy reads zero here: this host offloads the simulation, and the actor's
# snapshots carry no energy at the mere revision turnstone pins. What the
# restless law still owes is a layout with nothing stacked.
assert overlaps == 0
capture 02_add_orbit

# --- Charge: separates, and leaves nothing stacked ---
act Physics: Charge
settle 60
assert row Physics: Charge
open mere://p4/add/charge
wait
assert overlaps == 0

# --- Still: the law holds everything, the newcomer included ---
act Physics: Still
settle 60
assert row Physics: Still
open mere://p4/add/still
wait
assert overlaps == 0
capture 03_add_still
log physics add native receipt complete
